`,d.jsx(e.p,{children:"Every time you execute a database optimization strategy, you are making a prediction about human and application behavior. You are making an architectural bet that your users will run a specific category of queries often enough to justify penalizing your system's writes, memory, or storage overhead today."}),`
`,d.jsxs(e.p,{children:["When an engineer says, ",d.jsx(e.em,{children:'"Choose the right index,"'})," they are really prompting a deeper operational question:"]}),`
